 "what": "print-first redesign for a Bambu Lab A1 (0.4 mm nozzle), after the first print of the A2 core failed (guard top rings broke when the supports were removed). Compared at RM 52: A2 ring guards (2026-11-08), proposal P1 (band guard, pointed arches, 45 deg flare) and the adopted P2 wave guard (S ribbon 2.2 mm, 1.2 mm outward bulge, 45 deg ramps with a 1.2 mm rim, closed wire eyelets on the arms). 2026-11-13: P3 = P2 with one-piece motor holders (foot ring, wire channel, no landing loop), spokes flush with the rim top, rim-section bridges, wire holes in the arms, remeshed arm roots (adopted). Rev R (2026-11-13 evening): the core regenerated from a parametric plan as one smooth body (no mesh surgery), ring beam (deck ribs + raised rails with round caps), holder foot at z -30, clean STL for the slicer (adopted). Rev M (2026-11-15): modular frame printed without supports: body (deck on the bed), 4 guard baskets (guard top on the bed), 4 motor cups with the deck strut (flange on the bed); one-piece battery + flow tray printed upside down (adopted).",
